From: Prathyusha Potlapally <prathyusha@micasnetworks.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: print a practice startup marker

Print one notice when bgpd starts so the build, install and restart
workflow can be exercised in a lab. This is a learning change only.

diff --git a/bgpd/bgp_main.c b/bgpd/bgp_main.c
--- a/bgpd/bgp_main.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgp_main.c
@@ -566,6 +566,8 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 	/* must be called after fork() */
 	bgp_gr_apply_running_config();
 	bgp_pthreads_run();
+	zlog_notice("BGP-LEARNING-TEST: custom bgpd build started (Prathyusha)");
+
 	frr_run(bm->master);
 
 	/* Not reached. */
